{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And you shall rejoice in all the good.</b> From here our Rabbis said in Pesachim in the chapter כל שעה: from Shavuot until the Festival one brings and recites, for this is the time of bringing first fruits, and therefore Shavuot is called the Day of First Fruits. And all produce becomes first-ripe between these two seasons. From the Festival until Hanukkah one brings but does not recite, for there are still fruits, but it is not applicable to say ״הנה הבאתי מראשית פרי האדמה״, for now there is no first. From Hanukkah onward one neither brings nor recites, for it is written ״אשר תביא מארצך״, and now there is nothing at all, for even the grass of the field is consumed by that time." "<b>And the stranger who is in your midst.</b> The question arose to the Rav Rabbi Yosef Kara: what is the relevance of a stranger to first fruits, when first fruits are given only to priests? And furthermore, ״אשר תביא מארצך״ is written, to exclude strangers who have no portion in the land — until there came before Rabbi Yom Tov, and he showed him a clear midrash and proof in tractate Bikkurim in the chapter אלו מביאים ולא קורין: that they cannot say ״אשר נשבע לאבותינו לתת לנו״. A stranger — if his mother was not from Israel — brings but does not recite, and when he prays privately he says: 'God of the fathers of Israel.' And if his mother was from Israel he says: 'Our God and God of our fathers.' And on this they cited a mishnah in the Jerusalem Talmud: Rabbi Abbahu taught in the name of Rabbi Yehudah: a stranger himself brings and recites. What is the reason? ״כי אב המון גוים נתתיך״ — until now you were a father to Aram; from here onward, a father to all the nations. Rabbi Yehoshua ben Levi said: the halakhah follows Rabbi Yehudah. A case came before Rabbi [and he] ruled like Rabbi Yehudah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:28.380748839Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}